of a body about a given axis is <math><mn>1.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Initially the body is at rest. In order to produce a rotational kinetic energy of <math><mn>1200</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the angular acceleration of <math><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> must be applied about the axis for a duration of:"}, "options": [{"id": "e9040e", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f00"}, {"id": "f01763", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f01"}, {"id": "2f1323", "text": "<math><mn>2.5</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f02"}, {"id": "17885e", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f03"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f04", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "A thin circular disc of mass $M$ and radius $R$ is rotating in a horizontal plane about an axis passing through its centre and perpendicular to its plane with angular velocity $\\omega$. If another disc of same dimensions but of mass $\\mathrm{M} / 2$ is placed gently on the first disc co-axially, then the new angular velocity of the system is :"}, "options": [{"id": "96ba34", "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} \\omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f05"}, {"id": "addc06", "text": "$\\frac{5}{4} \\omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f06"}, {"id": "9e71bc", "text": "$\\frac{2}{3} \\omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f07"}, {"id": "0d9d37", "text": "$\\frac{4}{5} \\omega$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f08"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f09", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "A solid cylinder and a solid sphere, having same mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, roll down the same inclined plane from top without slipping. They start from rest. The ratio of velocity of the solid cylinder to that of the solid sphere, with which they reach the ground, will be"}, "options": [{"id": "04d8ad", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0a"}, {"id": "e0dde1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0b"}, {"id": "facc3c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0c"}, {"id": "9da6bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9259"], "question": {"text": "<p>Shown in the figure is a hollow ice-cream cone (it is open at top). If its mass is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>, radius of its top is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;and height,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>, then its moment of inertia about its axis is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Feb02c1ca-ac0e-48eb-9505-899ed438a4f7-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 152px; height: 260px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f7fd60", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f0f"}, {"id": "95ab4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f10"}, {"id": "245648", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MH</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f11"}, {"id": "dab13e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>MR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f12"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f13", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cad"], "question": {"text": "An object of mass ' m ' is projected from origin in a vertical $x y$ plane at an angle $45^{\\circ}$ with the x axis with an initial velocity $\\mathrm{v}_0$. The magnitude and direction of the angular momentum of the object with respect to origin, when it reaches at the maximum height, will be [ g is acceleration due to gravity]"}, "options": [{"id": "cc96cb", "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{2 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along negative $z$-axis", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f14"}, {"id": "8ab12a", "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{4 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along positive $z$-axis", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f15"}, {"id": "80003f", "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{4 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along negative $z$-axis", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f16"}, {"id": "abc3fc", "text": "$\\frac{m v_o^3}{2 \\sqrt{2} g}$ along positive $z$-axis", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f17"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f18", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["6117b76a478ae845c43c6d48"], "question": {"text": "Two masses <math><mi>m</mi></math> and <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> are connected at the two ends of a massless rigid rod of length <math><mi>l</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The rod is suspended by a thin wire of torsional constant <math><mi>k</mi></math> at the centre of mass of the rod-mass system (see figure). Because of torsional constant <math><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the restoring torque is <math><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math> for angular displacement <math><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the rod is rotated by <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> and released, the tension in it when it passes through its mean position will be:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fkednmqfmibhfvsssekvrbkqvkijjcgvwoiknielqwngahcrjng.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "a6fd73", "text": "<math><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f19"}, {"id": "b23375", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1a"}, {"id": "512c24", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1b"}, {"id": "be617e", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "A cord is wound round the circumference of wheel of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mi></mi></math>, The axis of the wheel is horizontal and the moment of inertia about it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>. A weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math> is attached to the cord at the end. The weight falls from rest. After falling through a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the square of angular velocity of wheel will be"}, "options": [{"id": "cf0dc5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1e"}, {"id": "b3176f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f1f"}, {"id": "5e6b41", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f20"}, {"id": "2952e7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f21"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f22", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473f"], "question": {"text": "a string is wound around a hollow cylinder of mass $5 \\mathrm{~kg}$ and radius $0.5 \\mathrm{~m}$. If the string is now pulled with a horizontal force of $40 \\mathrm{~N}$, and the cylinder is rolling without slipping on a horizontal surface (see figure), then the angular acceleration of the cylinder will be (Neglect the mass and thickness of the string)\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FlhYbJyMOwbm_eO2pTm220FwNnlXmd22hwTtWbUx6zxM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">"}, "options": [{"id": "8541b3", "text": "$20 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f23"}, {"id": "43df6d", "text": "$16 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f24"}, {"id": "20687d", "text": "$12 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f25"}, {"id": "91f29e", "text": "$10 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f26"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f27", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b94a67dbe2603c3e992e"], "question": {"text": "The radius of gyration of a uniform rod of length <math><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> about an axis passing through a point <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> away from the centre of the rod, and perpendicular to it, is:"}, "options": [{"id": "c69a10", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>l</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f28"}, {"id": "742603", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>l</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f29"}, {"id": "1988cb", "text": "<math><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>48</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mi>l</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2a"}, {"id": "bcc9e6", "text": "<math><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mi>l</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ad"], "question": {"text": "A heavy iron bar, of weight $W$ is having its one end on the ground and the other on the shoulder of a person. The bar makes an angle $\\theta$ with the horizontal. The weight experienced by the person is :"}, "options": [{"id": "2c22a6", "text": "$\\mathrm{W} \\cos \\theta$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2d"}, {"id": "9a1257", "text": "$\\frac{W}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2e"}, {"id": "d96a06", "text": "W", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f2f"}, {"id": "10e8d2", "text": "$W \\sin \\theta$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f30"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f31", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e49"], "question": {"text": "A uniform solid cylinder of mass ' $m$ ' and radius ' $r$ ' rolls along an inclined rough plane of inclination $45^{\\circ}$. If it starts to roll from rest from the top of the plane then the linear acceleration of the cylinder's axis will be"}, "options": [{"id": "a1f04c", "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\mathrm{~g}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f32"}, {"id": "d659b8", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3 \\sqrt{2}} \\mathrm{~g}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f33"}, {"id": "7852ff", "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~g}}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f34"}, {"id": "cddd65", "text": "$\\sqrt{2} g$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f35"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f36", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0f"], "question": {"text": "A thin circular ring of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is rotating with a constant angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in a horizontal plane about an axis vertical to its plane and passing through the center of the ring. If two objects each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> be attached gently to the opposite ends of a diameter of ring, the ring will then rotate with an angular velocity (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)."}, "options": [{"id": "fdd995", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f37"}, {"id": "fdd061", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f38"}, {"id": "3b5d75", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f39"}, {"id": "1397da", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "<p>A disc of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is rolling horizontally without slipping with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. It then moves up an inclined smooth surface as shown in figure. The maximum height that the disc can go up the incline is:</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F85a09b36-4b67-4c39-b4b7-bb08bcfe1dda.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 122px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "8dba5c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3c"}, {"id": "6363ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3d"}, {"id": "157d6e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3e"}, {"id": "057abf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f3f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f40", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a0"], "question": {"text": "The linear mass density of a thin rod&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math>&nbsp;of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;varies from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is the distance from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;is the mass of the rod then its moment of inertia&nbsp;about an axis passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and perpendicular to the rod :"}, "options": [{"id": "7f2da8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f41"}, {"id": "4afce1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f42"}, {"id": "61f6d4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f43"}, {"id": "7c75e7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f44"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f45", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["6162faea6ed13040ec848e8c"], "question": {"text": "<p>A huge circular arc of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ly</mi></math> subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> at the centre of the circle. How long it would take for a body to complete <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> revolution if its speed is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AU</mi></math> per second?<br />Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ly</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AU</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "503f57", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f46"}, {"id": "d39108", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f47"}, {"id": "aa5171", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f48"}, {"id": "db8c05", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f49"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "The torque of a force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> about the origin is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math>. If the force acts on a particle whose position vector is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math> will be"}, "options": [{"id": "f5dc41", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4b"}, {"id": "e1d50d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4c"}, {"id": "8de0d6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4d"}, {"id": "800469", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f4f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cad"], "question": {"text": "<p>Four point masses, each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, are fixed at the corners of a square of side I. The square is rotating with angular frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>,</mo></math> about an axis passing through one of the corners of the square and parallel to tis diagonal, as shown in the figure. The angular momentum of the square about the axis is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fcd5726f9-83e6-4534-b914-9bc74c86b000-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 239px; height: 230px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "218bc4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f50"}, {"id": "5434b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f51"}, {"id": "4b776a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f52"}, {"id": "234d98", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mi>&#8467;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f53"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f54", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "Consider a situation in which a ring, a solid cylinder and a solid sphere roll down on the same inclined plane without slipping. Assume that they start rolling from rest and having identical diameter. The correct statement for this situation is&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "3b9618", "text": "The sphere has the greatest and the ring has the least velocity of the centre of mass at the bottom of the inclined plane.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f55"}, {"id": "0c8d27", "text": "The ring has the greatest and the cylinder has the least velocity of the centre of mass at the bottom of the inclined plane.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f56"}, {"id": "fab744", "text": "All of them will have same velocity.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f57"}, {"id": "b2d4cd", "text": "The cylinder has the greatest and the sphere has the least velocity of the centre of mass at the bottom of the inclined plane.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f58"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.292Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.292Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fbd"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fb9", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f98", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e45"], "question": {"text": "If a solid sphere of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and a disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> have the same radius, then the ratio of moment of inertia of the disc about a tangent in its plane to the moment of inertia of the sphere about its tangent will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "00b15c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f99"}, {"id": "208820", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9a"}, {"id": "a75347", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9b"}, {"id": "34b465", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e110"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0e3"], "question": {"text": "A metre scale is balanced on a knife edge at its centre. When two coins, each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> are put one on the top of the other at the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark the scale is found to be balanced at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark. The mass of the metre scale is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "2cc2c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9e"}, {"id": "d4716c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f9f"}, {"id": "74c6a0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa0"}, {"id": "820bf2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1e9d"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "One end of a straight uniform <math><mn>1</mn><mi></mi><mi>m</mi></math> long bar is pivoted on horizontal table. It is released from rest when it makes an angle <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> from the horizontal (see figure). Its angular speed when it hits the table is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> , where <math><mi>n</mi></math> is an integer. The value of <math><mi>n</mi></math> is ____________<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fb4c6a5b4-1140-40c3-862c-00ef5c6d4f73.jpeg?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "8dd88b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa3"}, {"id": "e7916f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa4"}, {"id": "d0b5ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa5"}, {"id": "7dd1da", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f40"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cad"], "question": {"text": "<p>A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is moving in time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;on a trajectory given by,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are dimensional constants.</p><p>The angular momentum of the particle becomes the same as it was for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> at time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_____ seconds.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "366f90", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa8"}, {"id": "b9fd2a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fa9"}, {"id": "c7c404", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255faa"}, {"id": "48b81d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fac", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df82"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4788"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cae"], "question": {"text": "A ring and a solid sphere roll down the same inclined plane without slipping. They start from rest. The radii of both bodies are identical and the ratio of their kinetic energies is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "8d477a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fad"}, {"id": "c738c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fae"}, {"id": "ff5060", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255faf"}, {"id": "f4366a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fb0"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.371Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:15.371Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255fbe"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:54.795Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:58.368Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e22e56cfac5cf3a1d8f", "testId": "69de21ea7e39d99b57bc5aa6", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:04:34.732Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 50, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f3b2ee0e063d9255f70"